  "report": "# F001 generate-verify-repair: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n- mutation check: 24 of 24 killed\n\nLimitations: the generator and the repairer are seeded stubs with a stated per-slot skill; the strict comparative rules (repair gains at least one success and saves at least one milli-draw per success over rewrite-only at every budget above one; the analytic gains are thousands) are consequences of that stated skill and test the loop's use of verdicts and critiques, not that any model repairs better than it rewrites; the task is synthetic: seven independent defect slots of an ActionIr against a fixed ActionContract; real generations have correlated, partial and unnamed defects, and a real repair is not a redraw of the named slot; the verifier noise (Unknown, Disputed, shallow, lying, forged) is scripted per call from the seed and independent of the candidate; the real learned and statistical verifiers are not exercised, and a verifier that lies by reporting a clean Pass for a defective candidate cannot be detected by the loop (only a self-contradicting Pass is refused); the cost measure is the number of slot draws and verifier calls, not tokens, latency or money; one verifier call costs the same whatever it verifies; the negative controls run the harness' own reference loop, not the product: they show the counters can fail, not that a defective product is caught; that evidence is the mutation plan; the expectation check uses 5 standard deviations because it makes several hundred comparisons per seed; a defect that shifts a success, call or draw count by less than that is not detected by it, only by the other counters; all arms of a task share their random draws (common random numbers) so that the comparative rules are tight; the arms are therefore not independent samples.\n"
}
